WEBVTT

00:00:00.143 --> 00:00:02.323
Information is CHEAP.

00:00:02.073 --> 00:00:04.243
Attention is NOT.

00:00:03.993 --> 00:00:07.263
Text, video, documents —

00:00:07.013 --> 00:00:11.601
the carriers of information cost almost nothing to make now.

00:00:11.351 --> 00:00:15.447
We live in a world DROWNING in information.

00:00:15.197 --> 00:00:16.769
Certainly at work.

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:21.371
But the passage from seeing something to UNDERSTANDING it —

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:24.129
that passage is still NARROW.

00:00:24.149 --> 00:00:26.539
As narrow as it's always been.

00:00:26.289 --> 00:00:28.310
Here is how I learned that.

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:29.723
I recently wrote a proposal.

00:00:29.473 --> 00:00:31.413
TEN pages.

00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:33.423
Every edge case.

00:00:33.443 --> 00:00:36.523
Every risk — with a mitigation plan for each.

00:00:36.273 --> 00:00:40.423
I didn't write a proposal. I wrote a MINI BOOK.

00:00:40.443 --> 00:00:42.443
My manager's feedback:

00:00:42.193 --> 00:00:46.432
"Too much detail. It is diluting your point.

00:00:46.182 --> 00:00:47.910
You LOST me."

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.430
And she was right.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:52.409
She cared. She just physically COULDN'T.

00:00:52.159 --> 00:00:55.569
I drowned her in detail.

00:00:55.319 --> 00:00:59.525
I asked for attention that NOBODY can afford.

00:00:59.275 --> 00:01:00.744
The proposal didn't pass.

00:01:00.494 --> 00:01:04.026
So here is my working theory:

00:01:04.046 --> 00:01:07.831
The hard skill in the AI era runs both ways:

00:01:07.851 --> 00:01:11.531
presenting information at the RIGHT level of attention —

00:01:11.281 --> 00:01:15.650
and spending our own attention on the RIGHT information.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:18.488
Information will keep getting cheaper.

00:01:18.508 --> 00:01:20.928
Attention stays SCARCE.

00:01:20.678 --> 00:01:23.768
So, honest question:

00:01:23.518 --> 00:01:27.932
what's the longest document you ever sent

00:01:27.952 --> 00:01:29.200
that nobody actually READ?
